1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:09,241
A student in Prague I was born raised and I currently live here and this is what a day in my life looks like.
我是布拉格的一名学生。我在这里出生、长大，现在也住在这里，这就是我的一天。

2
00:00:09,241 --> 00:00:15,601
I live in a typical panelak building which are concrete apartment buildings outside of the city center.
我住在一栋典型的 panelak 预制公寓楼里，这种混凝土公寓通常位于市中心以外。

3
00:00:15,601 --> 00:00:22,751
They were built during the communist era and are found across central and eastern Europe.
它们建于共产主义时期，在中欧和东欧都能见到。

4
00:00:22,761 --> 00:00:29,041
Hello welcome to my apartment let me show you.
你好，欢迎来我的公寓，我带你看看。

5
00:00:29,041 --> 00:00:37,921
So I live in a two bedroom apartment with my boyfriend but I only moved in a couple of months ago so it's pretty new.
我和男朋友住在一套两居室里，不过我几个月前才搬进来，所以还挺新鲜的。

6
00:00:37,921 --> 00:00:44,921
I have my homemade uh mint from my grandma's garden.
我这儿有自己做的薄荷饮品，薄荷来自奶奶的花园。

7
00:00:44,921 --> 00:00:48,601
For breakfast I'm having this pie that my mom made for me.
早餐我要吃妈妈给我做的这个派。

8
00:00:48,601 --> 00:00:59,681
The average age for Czechs to leave home is about 26 years which is typical across the eu according to Eurostat.
根据原片引用的欧盟统计局数据，捷克人平均大约二十六岁离家，这在欧盟范围内很常见。

9
00:00:59,681 --> 00:01:07,521
I mean if people live in the city where they also study the university I think they usually stay with their parents.
如果大家在自己居住的城市上大学，我觉得通常就还会和父母一起住。

10
00:01:07,521 --> 00:01:12,641
I mean I would stay with my parents if it wasn't for my partner.
要不是因为我的伴侣，我也会继续和父母住。

11
00:01:12,641 --> 00:01:19,201
These days one person apartment in the city center can cost around 700 to 1,000 per month.
按原片当时的说法，市中心一人住的公寓每月大约要七百到一千。

12
00:01:19,201 --> 00:01:27,241
Between 2022 and 20 23 rent prices increased by 20 and continue to go up.
原片说，二〇二二到二〇二三年间，房租涨了百分之二十，而且还在继续上涨。

13
00:01:27,241 --> 00:01:36,961
So I was invited for a panel discussion and a lecture because of my work so come with me.
因为我的工作，有人邀请我去参加一场小组讨论和讲座，跟我来吧。

14
00:01:36,961 --> 00:01:41,801
It's the velvet revolution week this week so I'm already wearing my ribbon.
这周是纪念天鹅绒革命的一周，所以我已经戴上了丝带。

15
00:01:41,801 --> 00:02:00,280
The velvet revolution took place in 1989 where the Czechs protested against the communist regime which eventually fell and now we live in a democracy.
天鹅绒革命发生在一九八九年，捷克民众抗议当时的共产主义政权，后来政权结束了，现在我们生活在民主制度下。

16
00:02:00,280 --> 00:02:09,441
We have one of the best public transport systems in Europe with buses trams metros and trains connecting the city and its outskirts.
这里的公共交通系统很发达，公交、有轨电车、地铁和火车把市区与周边连接起来。

17
00:02:09,441 --> 00:02:21,511
It is available 24/7 and it's incredibly cheap for students.
原片说，公共交通全天运行，学生乘坐也非常便宜。

18
00:02:21,521 --> 00:02:26,601
I do have my driver's license I got it when I was 18 years old and I think that's the norm for Czech people.
我有驾照，是十八岁时拿到的。我觉得这在捷克人中挺普遍的。

19
00:02:26,601 --> 00:02:31,001
You get your first official Czech beer and then you also get your driver's license.
到了那个年纪，你第一次正式喝捷克啤酒，也拿到了驾照。

20
00:02:31,001 --> 00:02:40,120
I don't necessarily use it I just think it's a good skill to have I guess but I don't really need a car in Prague.
我并不一定会用到驾照，只是觉得会开车是项不错的技能；在布拉格其实不太需要车。

21
00:02:40,120 --> 00:02:53,190
I'm a political science student but besides that I'm also a full time influencer or greenfluencer if you wish.
我学政治学，不过除此以外，我也是全职内容创作者，或者说环保领域的博主。

22
00:02:53,200 --> 00:03:06,400
I post about sustainability and climate and science and I'm trying to get people involved in the talks about overcoming climate change and other sustainable issues.
我分享可持续发展、气候和科学内容，希望让大家参与到应对气候变化及其他可持续议题的讨论中。
